exec
/usr/bin/bash -lc "cat > /tmp/codex-pr-455-review.md <<'EOF'
MUST-FIX

1. "'`packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte:192`
Global `ArrowLeft` / `ArrowRight` handling runs even when the reasoning textarea is focused. That means caret movement in the textarea navigates to another card and `resetForm()` clears the in-progress reasoning. Keyboard shortcuts need to ignore input/textarea/contenteditable targets (and typically modified keys) before triggering card navigation.

2. `packages/web-ui/src/lib/api-static.ts:407`
AC-8 says static mode should display triage decisions read-only, but `fetchTriageRecordsStatic()` always returns an empty list. In static mode the UI can never show existing triage decisions, so the implementation does not meet the AC as written. Either include triage records in static snapshots/load them here, or update the spec/AC + tests to reflect the limitation.

SHOULD-FIX

3. `tests/web-ui-triage.test.ts:166`
The AC-8 test only checks that write controls are hidden and the fallback message exists. It does not assert the "triage decisions display read-only" part of the AC, which is why the static-mode regression above still passes.

4. `tests/web-ui-triage.test.ts:268`
`@interactive-triage-ui` inherits `@trait-websocket-protocol` ac-1 through ac-8, but this file only has explicit trait AC annotations for ac-1..ac-3. If this requirement is expected to carry the full trait coverage annotation set, the missing ac-4..ac-8 annotations should be added (or the inheritance/coverage expectation should be clarified).

Notes

- `kspec task get @implement-interactive-triage-ui` and `kspec item get @interactive-triage-ui` reviewed.
- `kspec validate` passes (no trait coverage warnings emitted locally).
- `pnpm vitest tests/web-ui-triage.test.ts --run` passes (18 tests), but these are static-analysis/string-match tests and do not exercise runtime behavior.
